{% extends "base.html.j2" %}

{% block title %}Publishers &mdash; {{ config.site.title }}{% endblock %}

{% block meta %}
{% set social_title = 'Publishers' %}
{% set social_url = config.site.base_url ~ '/publisher/' %}
{% set social_description %}Who publishes the proceedings of
  {{ publishers | sum(attribute='editions' | length) if false else total }} recorded
  editions, how much of it a reader can obtain without paying, and how much of
  it is openly licensed.{% endset %}
<meta name="description" content="{{ social_description | oneline }}">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ social_url }}">
{% include "_social.html.j2" %}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<article>

<header class="page-head">
  <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">All conferences</a> / Publishers</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Publishers</h1>
  <p class="page-sub">Who publishes {{ total }} recorded volumes, and on what
    terms.</p>
</header>

<section class="panel">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Choosing where to submit is also choosing a publisher, and that choice
      is usually made without seeing it stated. Three things are kept apart
      here, because they are different claims: whether a reader can obtain the
      paper <b>without paying</b>, whether it carries an <b>open licence</b>,
      and whether the <b>authors keep their rights</b>. A publisher can satisfy
      one and fail the others, and several do.</p>
    <p>A fourth thing is not recorded anywhere on this site and is worth
      naming: <b>who paid</b>. Where a commercial publisher issues a paper
      under an open licence, the charge has usually moved to the author rather
      than disappeared. Those volumes look spotless on all three axes above.
      The publisher's own page says so in full.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel">
  <table class="editions sortable" id="pubindex">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th data-sort="text">Publisher</th>
        <th class="num" data-sort="number" aria-sort="descending">Volumes</th>
        <th class="num" data-sort="number">Confs</th>
        <th class="num" data-sort="number">Free to read</th>
        <th class="num" data-sort="number">Open licence</th>
        <th data-sort="text">Commercial</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for p in publishers %}
      <tr>
        <td><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.name }}</a>
          {%- if p.diamond %} <span class="diamond" title="Open licence and not for profit: no charge to the reader, none to the author">&#9733;</span>{% endif %}
          {%- if not p.known %} <small class="data">not in publishers.toml</small>{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ p.editions | length }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ p.conferences | length }}</td>
        {# A bar as well as the figure: the length is what makes a column of
           eighty rows scannable, and the number is what keeps the colour from
           carrying the meaning on its own. #}
        {# Three fixed slots — figure, bar, denominator — so a row carrying
           "of 102" does not shunt its percentage out of line with the rest. #}
        {% for value, band in ((p.free_pct, p.free_band), (p.open_pct, p.open_band)) %}
        <td class="num">
          <span class="pctcell">
            {%- if value is not none %}<span class="pctnum">{{ value }}%</span>
            <span class="meter" data-band="{{ band }}"><i style="--w: {{ value }}%"></i></span>
            <span class="pctof">{% if p.rated != p.editions | length %}of {{ p.rated }}{% endif %}</span>
            {%- else %}<span class="pctnum">&ndash;</span><span class="meter"></span>
            <span class="pctof"></span>{% endif %}</span></td>
        {% endfor %}
        <td>{% if p.commercial %}<span class="commercial" data-profit="yes">for profit</span>
          {%- elif p.commercial is false %}<span class="commercial" data-profit="no">non-profit</span>
          {%- else %}<a class="data unanswered" href="#unanswered">not recorded</a>{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="chart-caption">
    Bars run red below 10%, through orange and amber, to green at 95% and
    above; the figure beside each one is there so the colour is never the only
    thing saying it.
    <span class="diamond">&#9733;</span> marks a publisher that charges neither
    the reader nor the author: an open licence across its volumes <i>and</i> a
    recorded answer that it is not for profit. Both halves have to be stated to
    earn it &mdash; an unrecorded <code>for_profit</code> is not a denial, which
    is also why a row can read <i>not recorded</i> there while being perfectly
    well described otherwise. That is a gap in this site, not a judgement about the
    publisher. Where a publisher's figures rest on fewer volumes than it has
    here, the shortfall is printed beside the bar.</p>
</section>

{% if unanswered %}
<section class="panel" id="unanswered">
  <h2 class="panel-title">Publishers with no answer on <code>for_profit</code></h2>
  <p class="chart-caption">The <i>Commercial</i> column is only as useful as
    this list is short. {{ unanswered_count }} publishers here, carrying
    {{ unanswered_volumes }} of {{ total }} volumes, have no
    <code>for_profit</code> line in <code>publishers.toml</code> &mdash; so the
    site cannot say either way, and does not. Most of them are otherwise
    described; the field simply was not filled in. The twelve carrying the most
    volumes are below, since answering those covers most of the corpus.</p>
  <ul class="nearly">
    {% for p in unanswered %}
    <li>
      <a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.name }}</a>
      <span class="data">{{ p.editions | length }} volume{{ 's' if p.editions | length != 1 }}</span>
      <span class="nearly-holes">{{ p.conferences | length }} series</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  <p class="chart-caption">One line each: <code>for_profit = true</code> or
    <code>for_profit = false</code>. It is a claim about the publisher, never
    about any one edition's licence (&sect;&nbsp;6 of the schema).</p>
</section>
{% endif %}

</article>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
<script src="/assets/places.js?v={{ asset_version }}" defer></script>
{% endblock %}
